Q: How to make text and image columns have equal height A: <p>Assuming the image is not too wide, it is possible with CSS. Otherwise, it will get cropped.</p>
<p>Basically, the image gets <code>height: 100%</code> and <code>width: auto</code>. The text should fill the space with <code>flex-grow: 1</code>. It all depends on too many factors, if known the answer can be improved.</p>
<p>Here are few examples:</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>.parent {
  display: flex;
  border: 1px solid red;
  height: 150px;
  width: 400px;
  gap: 20px;
  margin-bottom: 20px;
}

.left {
  background: green;
  font-size: 3em;
  text-align: center;
  flex: 1;
  border-radius: 20px;
}

.right {
  border-radius: 20px;
  overflow: hidden;
}

.right img {
  height: 100%;
  width: auto;
}</code></pre>
